		<note type="caution">
			<p>When replacing tires, use the same size originally supplied with the vehicle.</p>
			<p>Using tires of a different size can damage the related parts or make it work irregularly.</p>
		</note>
		<note type="note">
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p>We recommend that when replacing tires, use the same originally supplied with the vehicles.</p>
					<p>If not, that affects driving performance.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>When driving in high altitude grades, it is natural for the atmospheric pressure to decrease.</p>
					<p>Therefore, please check the tire pressure and add more air when necessary.</p>
					<p>Additionally required tire air pressure per km above sea level: 1.5 psi/km</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
